Please treat this as the issue receipt for revision C of RC-17. Revision B
is withdrawn. The pages marked D-draft have been circulated for comment
but have not been issued, regardless of their later file timestamps.

The page order for the archive service is the SERVICE_ORDER on the appliance
label. The scanner has mixed the copies again, so the order in the text
export tells us nothing. The four footer strips are the recovery material;
the section headings decide where each strip goes.

Also, the final desk phrase is not "Back before the first boat" or the
standby envelope's "Leave the light on for the next watch." Those labels
survive in the crew notes because I kept the old drafts. For this envelope
I wanted the line that felt like people making room for each other after
a long watch, with the water outside and the night almost finished. The
desk notes and photograph captions were how I worked out the wording.

Emily
